==Enemy==
This Easter variant of [[Duche]] has a cracked egg on her head and carries a bowl of eggs on her back. Compared to Duche, she's HUGE! Luckily, her damage doesn't match her size, doing only 3,600 damage at 100% strength magnification, along with having two knockbacks. She does have rather high health, though, especially at higher magnifications.

==Strategy==
With her impressive health and decent range, she mainly serves as a high-health wall that does just enough damage to keep away most [[:Category:Midranger-class Cats|midrangers]], like [[Mer-Cat (Rare Cat)|Cameraman Cat]], [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]] and non-[[True Form]] [[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Ring Girl Cat]]. This means you'll have to use higher range Cats, like Pizza Cat, [[Surfer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Castaway Cat]], [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Bahamut Cat]] or [[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|Dual]] [[Crazed Lizard Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Dragons]]. Additionally, although Easter Duche is meant to be a wall, she lacks any immunities, so she can be crowd-controlled by Cats like [[Lifeguard Cats (Super Rare Cat)|Sweet Bro Cats]], [[Glass Cat (Rare Cat)|Macho Glass Cat]], [[Lone Cat and Kitten (Rare Cat)|Vendor Cat and Kitten]], and [[Jagando Jr. (Special Cat)|Lord of Ruin Jagando Jr.]].

